{
  "sn22.101:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.101 ",
  "sn22.101:0.2": "10. Flowers ",
  "sn22.101:0.3": "The Adze ",
  "sn22.101:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn22.101:1.2": "“Mendicants, I say that the ending of defilements is for one who knows and sees, not for one who does not know or see. ",
  "sn22.101:1.3": "For one who knows and sees what? ",
  "sn22.101:1.4": "‘Such is form, such is the origin of form, such is the disappearance of form. ",
  "sn22.101:1.5": "Such is feeling … ",
  "sn22.101:1.6": "Such is perception … ",
  "sn22.101:1.7": "Such are choices … ",
  "sn22.101:1.8": "Such is consciousness, such is the origin of consciousness, such is the disappearance of consciousness.’ ",
  "sn22.101:1.9": "The ending of the defilements is for one who knows and sees this. ",
  "sn22.101:2.1": "When a mendicant is not committed to development, they might wish: ",
  "sn22.101:2.2": "‘If only my mind were freed from the defilements by not grasping!’ Even so, their mind is not freed from defilements by not grasping. ",
  "sn22.101:2.3": "Why is that? ",
  "sn22.101:2.4": "You should say: ‘It’s because they’re undeveloped.’ ",
  "sn22.101:2.5": "Undeveloped in what? ",
  "sn22.101:2.6": "Undeveloped in the four kinds of mindfulness meditation, the four right efforts, the four bases of psychic power, the five faculties, the five powers, the seven awakening factors, and the noble eightfold path. ",
  "sn22.101:3.1": "Suppose there was a chicken with eight or ten or twelve eggs. ",
  "sn22.101:3